1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,007
Last time, you wrote one quest,

2
00:00:02,457 --> 00:00:04,206
and a quest is a task.

3
00:00:05,106 --> 00:00:07,808
This is a story, with a beginning, a middle,

4
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:10,264
and an ending you can win or lose.

5
00:00:11,164 --> 00:00:14,122
It's still one text file, and it's still no code.

6
00:00:15,022 --> 00:00:17,273
And the quest you wrote last time

7
00:00:17,723 --> 00:00:19,663
is going to be its first step.

8
00:00:21,463 --> 00:00:22,807
A story needs a heading,

9
00:00:23,257 --> 00:00:26,466
and it's made the way every heading is:

10
00:00:26,916 --> 00:00:29,454
three hashes, a name, and a key.

11
00:00:30,354 --> 00:00:33,226
Inside the fence there's one word on a line by itself,

12
00:00:33,676 --> 00:00:36,368
the word Arc, with no colon after it.

13
00:00:37,268 --> 00:00:39,596
What that word says is,

14
00:00:40,046 --> 00:00:43,563
I'm not a task, I'm the heading over some tasks.

15
00:00:45,363 --> 00:00:46,792
The rest you've seen before:

16
00:00:47,242 --> 00:00:49,663
it's shared, it starts at once,

17
00:00:50,113 --> 00:00:53,534
and below the fence there's one line of story.

18
00:00:54,734 --> 00:00:57,621
Now for the trick, and it's just one more hash.

19
00:00:58,521 --> 00:01:03,167
Four hashes means, I'm a step of the three-hash record above me.

20
00:01:04,067 --> 00:01:06,065
And that's all nesting is.

21
00:01:07,865 --> 00:01:09,638
So Close Inspection was a quest,

22
00:01:10,088 --> 00:01:12,831
and now it's step one of Salvage Run,

23
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:17,167
which gives it a full address: salvage, slash, approach.

24
00:01:18,367 --> 00:01:21,943
Step two goes here, and not at the bottom of the section.

25
00:01:22,843 --> 00:01:28,507
That's because a four-hash step belongs to the nearest three-hash heading above it,

26
00:01:28,957 --> 00:01:31,802
and my quest from last time is a three-hash heading.

27
00:01:32,702 --> 00:01:33,935
So if I type below it,

28
00:01:34,385 --> 00:01:36,674
my new step joins the wrong story,

29
00:01:37,124 --> 00:01:39,224
and the game is won at the first step.

30
00:01:41,024 --> 00:01:42,592
Lint does warn about that,

31
00:01:43,042 --> 00:01:44,951
and I'll show you the warning at the end,

32
00:01:45,401 --> 00:01:46,699
because it comes with a trap.

33
00:01:47,599 --> 00:01:51,277
Now, this line is new: Starts when, revealed.

34
00:01:52,177 --> 00:01:56,739
It means this step is hidden and asleep, until something wakes it.

35
00:01:57,939 --> 00:02:00,360
Nothing wakes it yet, and lint knows that.

36
00:02:01,260 --> 00:02:03,179
It read the word revealed,

37
00:02:03,629 --> 00:02:08,283
went looking for the line that reveals this step, and found none.

38
00:02:09,183 --> 00:02:11,163
Now read to the end of the warning,

39
00:02:11,613 --> 00:02:13,642
because it writes the line out for me,

40
00:02:14,092 --> 00:02:17,684
and the line begins Then, reveal.

41
00:02:18,584 --> 00:02:22,261
That says, when Close Inspection finishes, start that one.

42
00:02:23,161 --> 00:02:26,564
Notice it's the full address, arc, slash, step,

43
00:02:27,014 --> 00:02:28,581
and not just the word home.

44
00:02:29,481 --> 00:02:31,837
And a quest gets one Then line, no more.

45
00:02:33,637 --> 00:02:37,167
So I add it, I save, and lint says clean.

46
00:02:38,067 --> 00:02:42,326
That's a chain: you finish one, and the next begins.

47
00:02:43,526 --> 00:02:47,641
Next comes a bonus: reach the hulk inside two minutes.

48
00:02:48,541 --> 00:02:50,495
It has a Done when line,

49
00:02:50,945 --> 00:02:53,778
and it has the opposite, Fails when,

50
00:02:54,228 --> 00:02:57,012
and whichever comes first decides it.

51
00:02:57,912 --> 00:03:00,378
So if the crew is quick, they're paid fifty.

52
00:03:00,828 --> 00:03:03,709
If they're slow, the step fails,

53
00:03:04,159 --> 00:03:05,547
and that's all that happens.

54
00:03:06,747 --> 00:03:10,461
As it stands, the story waits for every step, the bonus included.

55
00:03:11,361 --> 00:03:13,912
So if the bonus failed, the story could never finish.

56
00:03:15,712 --> 00:03:18,401
That's why I say which steps count.

57
00:03:19,301 --> 00:03:23,140
I add two lines, Part of salvage, and Required true,

58
00:03:23,590 --> 00:03:27,822
on these two steps, and not on the bonus.

59
00:03:28,722 --> 00:03:30,356
And now the story is done

60
00:03:30,806 --> 00:03:32,489
when the required steps are done.

61
00:03:33,689 --> 00:03:36,517
There are two arcs in this file,

62
00:03:36,967 --> 00:03:39,787
and they start with the same three lines,

63
00:03:40,237 --> 00:03:42,022
so I make sure I'm in Salvage Run.

64
00:03:42,922 --> 00:03:45,067
First comes a time limit,

65
00:03:45,517 --> 00:03:47,016
then Win, with a sentence,

66
00:03:47,466 --> 00:03:49,474
and Lose, with a sentence.

67
00:03:50,374 --> 00:03:52,283
Win fires when this record is finished,

68
00:03:52,733 --> 00:03:54,921
and Lose fires when it fails.

69
00:03:56,721 --> 00:03:58,464
And here's the rule to remember:

70
00:03:58,914 --> 00:04:01,679
Fails when only fails a quest.

71
00:04:02,579 --> 00:04:05,667
It's Lose that makes a failure end the game.

72
00:04:07,467 --> 00:04:09,291
So I run lint, and it's clean.

73
00:04:10,491 --> 00:04:13,057
Now, there's one mistake I want you to see

74
00:04:13,507 --> 00:04:14,809
before you make it yourself:

75
00:04:15,259 --> 00:04:16,998
one hash too few on a step.

76
00:04:17,898 --> 00:04:21,184
Lint warns me, and it's talking about line sixty-five,

77
00:04:21,634 --> 00:04:25,234
which is my Then line, and not the heading I changed.

78
00:04:26,134 --> 00:04:29,037
You know that habit of lint's from Lecture 6.

79
00:04:29,937 --> 00:04:32,169
But look at how the sentence ends.

80
00:04:33,069 --> 00:04:35,199
It's found my step in its new place,

81
00:04:35,649 --> 00:04:38,883
and it offers me a new Then line that points there.

82
00:04:39,783 --> 00:04:41,864
If I write that, lint says clean,

83
00:04:42,314 --> 00:04:45,875
and the game is won the moment the crew reaches the hulk,

84
00:04:46,325 --> 00:04:48,913
because my story has only one step left.

85
00:04:50,713 --> 00:04:53,783
The Then line was right all along,

86
00:04:54,233 --> 00:04:56,635
and it was the heading that was wrong.

87
00:04:57,535 --> 00:05:00,414
So, when lint offers you a new Then line,

88
00:05:00,864 --> 00:05:03,253
count the hashes on the step first.

89
00:05:04,453 --> 00:05:06,745
Here's the Quest Log, with two steps showing,

90
00:05:07,195 --> 00:05:08,984
and the third one still hidden.

91
00:05:09,884 --> 00:05:12,079
So in we go, toward the hulk.

92
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,612
Close Inspection is done, and Quick Work is done with it.

93
00:05:16,512 --> 00:05:18,976
And there's step three, Bring the Log Home,

94
00:05:19,426 --> 00:05:21,042
so we turn for home.

95
00:05:21,942 --> 00:05:24,428
And that's the win, with my own sentence on it.

96
00:05:25,628 --> 00:05:28,004
Now I change ten minutes to thirty seconds,

97
00:05:28,454 --> 00:05:29,833
and I sit on my hands.

98
00:05:30,733 --> 00:05:33,800
And it's lost, with my other sentence.

99
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:36,878
Notice that nobody warned me.

100
00:05:37,778 --> 00:05:39,841
Your crew gets no countdown call,

101
00:05:40,291 --> 00:05:43,422
so tell them the limit in the arc's description,

102
00:05:43,872 --> 00:05:46,901
and tell them again in the first step's.

103
00:05:47,801 --> 00:05:49,780
And then I put ten minutes back.

104
00:05:50,980 --> 00:05:52,871
Now it's your turn: add a fourth step.

105
00:05:53,771 --> 00:05:55,718
It's revealed by the third,

106
00:05:56,168 --> 00:05:58,898
it's finished by a timer, and it's required.

107
00:05:59,798 --> 00:06:03,503
Then the win comes thirty seconds after they get home.

108
00:06:05,303 --> 00:06:07,667
Next time, we look at the things quests point at.
